{{!-- Which values the Inventar table shows.

A popover rather than a panel on the tab: the catalogue is long, it is consulted
rather than read, and twenty-two permanently visible checkboxes would cost the
table the width it exists to spend on data.

The sections mirror the item sheet's own blocks, so a column is looked for where
its field is authored. Nothing here is actor data — the choice is a client
setting and follows the reader to every sheet they open — which is why the
picker is offered on read-only sheets too. --}}
<div class='item-popover-head'>
  <h4>{{localize 'TNO.ItemTable.ColumnsTitle'}}</h4>
  <a data-columns-action='close' title='{{localize "TNO.ItemTable.Close"}}'>
    <i class='fas fa-xmark'></i>
  </a>
</div>

<p class='columns-popover-hint'>{{localize 'TNO.ItemTable.ColumnsHint'}}</p>

<div class='columns-popover-body'>
  {{#each sections as |section|}}
    <div class='columns-popover-section'>
      <h5>{{section.label}}</h5>
      {{#each section.columns as |column|}}
        <label class='columns-popover-row' title='{{column.hint}}'>
          <input type='checkbox' data-column='{{column.key}}' {{#if column.checked}}checked{{/if}} />
          <span>{{column.label}}</span>
        </label>
      {{/each}}
    </div>
  {{/each}}
</div>
